{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","book":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible","chapter":581,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:jfb:Ps.103","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","authorshipDateRange":"19th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Protestant","translator":null,"edition":"1871 one-volume text; expanded electronic edition by Ernie Stefanik","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"jfb","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"searchIndexed":false},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"jfb","source":{"id":"jfb","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"title":"Psalms 103","reference":"Psalms 103","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"PSALM 103","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Ps 103:1-22.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"A Psalm of joyous praise, in which the writer rises from a thankful acknowledgment of personal blessings to a lively celebration of God's gracious attributes, as not only intrinsically worthy of praise, but as specially suited to man's frailty.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"He concludes by invoking all creatures to unite in his song.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":5,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"Bless, &c.—when God is the object, praise.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"my soul—myself (Ps 3:3; 25:1), with allusion to the act, as one of intelligence.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"all … within me—(De 6:5).","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"his holy name—(Ps 5:11), His complete moral perfections.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"2. forget not all—not any, none of His benefits.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":11,"text":"3. diseases—as penal inflictions (De 29:22; 2Ch 21:19).","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"4. redeemeth—Cost is implied.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"destruction—literally, \"pit of corruption\" (Ps 16:10).","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"crowneth—or, \"adorneth\" (Ps 65:11).","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":15,"text":"tender mercies—compassions (compare Ps 25:6; 40:11).","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":16,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":17,"text":"By God's provision, the saint retains a youthful vigor like the eagles (Ps 92:14; compare Isa 40:31).","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":19,"text":"Literally, \"righteousness and judgments,\" denoting various acts of God's government.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":20,"text":"7. ways—of providence, &c., as usual (Ps 25:4; 67:2).","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":21,"text":"acts—literally, \"wonders\" (Ps 7:11; 78:17).","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":22,"text":"8-10.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":23,"text":"God's benevolence implies no merit.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":24,"text":"He shows it to sinners, who also are chastened for a time (Ex 34:6).","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":25,"text":"keep (anger)—in Le 19:18, bear a grudge (Jer 3:5, 12).","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":26,"text":"11. great—efficient.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":27,"text":"12. removed … from us—so as no longer to affect our relations to Him.","sourceParagraph":20,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":28,"text":"13. pitieth—literally, \"has compassion on.\"","sourceParagraph":21,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":29,"text":"14. he—\"who formed,\" Ps 94:9.","sourceParagraph":22,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":30,"text":"knoweth our frame—literally, \"our form.\"","sourceParagraph":23,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":31,"text":"we are dust—made of and tending to it (Ge 2:7).","sourceParagraph":24,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":32,"text":"15, 16.","sourceParagraph":25,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":33,"text":"So short and frail is life that a breath may destroy it.","sourceParagraph":25,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":34,"text":"it is gone—literally, \"it is not.\"","sourceParagraph":26,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":35,"text":"know it no more—no more recognize him (Ps 90:6; Isa 40:6-8).","sourceParagraph":27,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":36,"text":"17, 18.","sourceParagraph":28,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":37,"text":"For similar contrast compare Ps 90:2-6; 102:27, 28.","sourceParagraph":28,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":38,"text":"18. such … covenant—limits the general terms preceding.","sourceParagraph":29,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":39,"text":"righteousness—as usual (Ps 7:17; 31:1).","sourceParagraph":30,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":40,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":31,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":41,"text":"God's firm and universal dominion is a pledge that He will keep His promises (Ps 11:4; 47:8).","sourceParagraph":31,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":42,"text":"20-22. do his commandments … word—or, literally, \"so as to hearken,\" &c., that is, their acts of obedience are prompt, so that they are ever ready to hear, and know, and follow implicitly His declared will (compare De 26:17; Lu 1:19).","sourceParagraph":32,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":43,"text":"21. ye his hosts—myriads, or armies, as corresponding to angels of great power [Ps 103:20], denoting multitudes also.","sourceParagraph":33,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":44,"text":"22. all his works—creatures of every sort, everywhere.","sourceParagraph":34,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":103}}